abstract: >-
  babyseat is a local AI seat with a memory (membrane) that learns in real time:
  it sits in front of a local model server such as Ollama, and everything a person
  and their AI say passes through it and is parsed into per-entity memory as it
  happens. Inside lives Blurp, a small self that grows up on that memory one tested
  skill at a time, after Alan Turing's "child machine" idea; some of its skills
  work today and others are still being learned or rebuilt.
keywords:
